  "note": "Element-only 'Cu' = natural mixture. EasySpin's Sys.A is for the most abundant magnetic isotope (63Cu, isotopologues.m 'gnref'); 65Cu gets A * gn(65Cu)/gn(63Cu) = A * 1.0711880 (moments from isotopedata.txt at the fetched SHA; older EasySpin versions that wrote the .mat used slightly different moments, < 1e-4 relative). Abundances 69.17 / 30.83 %. EasySpin used full diagonalisation; second-order perturbation is the looser comparison. pepper's projection step (no strains) returns ref[i] ~ true(x[i] + dx/2): an independent converged powder sum matched axiallw, rhombiclw, ordering_axial row 0, pt_gonly, iso_12c and modamp best with the simulator evaluated at x + 0.5*dx (residual 4e-4 to 9e-3 there, 3e-2 to 2.7e-1 at x). The g-strain case (pepper's summation path) needs no offset.",
